  "executive_briefing": "As of mid-2026, global tax policy is dominated by the active statutory implementation of the OECD Pillar Two 15% global minimum tax regime across roughly 140 jurisdictions, forcing multinational enterprises to navigate GloBE top-up taxes and complex compliance standards. Parallelly, international trade environment volatility has peaked due to sweeping unilateral tariffs and trade measures, sparking legal and supply chain realignments. Regional financial centers, particularly in the ASEAN region, are adapting corporate tax incentive frameworks and non-taxable CIT rebates to preserve investment attractiveness despite minimum tax constraints. Simultaneously, tax administrations continue the rapid rollout of mandatory digital tax compliance frameworks, leveraging standard Peppol-based e-invoicing networks like Singapore's InvoiceNow to capture real-time GST/VAT transactional data.",
